   <!-- Usage added for FHIR-57188 -->
   <usage value="The composite score is calculated as the proportion of completed care opportunities across all applicable component measures. Each eligible component measure contributes one opportunity to the composite denominator, and each satisfied component numerator contributes one completed opportunity to the composite numerator. Denominator exclusions and exceptions are evaluated at the component measure level and remove the associated opportunity from the calculation. Risk adjustment variables X, Y, and Z are applied to the calculated composite performance rate."/>
